# IDE parity

The ax Command Center (`ax web`) must be available inside every IDE ax supports, installable from Settings -> IDEs & agents.

- VS Code family (Cursor, VS Code, Windsurf, Antigravity, Kiro): the bundled ax extension embeds `ax web?embed=1` in a panel.
- JetBrains: the bundled ax plugin embeds the same page in a tool window.
- IDEs without webview support (Zed): provide an `Open ax web` command that opens it in the browser.

When adding a new IDE target to `ax-installer`, add its Command Center integration in the same change.